# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
register_gate "tests/test_now_contended_change.py" "NOW CONTENDED-BY-CHANGE GATE: PASS" "the live Now banner is keyed on CHANGE, not author — one login's two PRs on a file collide (the gate serializes them) and surface" "NOW-CONTENDED-BY-CHANGE: now_for_installation's contended (the red 'N files colliding right now' banner) must reflect what the GATE serializes, which is keyed on the CHANGE not the author. The gate's holder check excludes only same-agent-AND-same-change, so ONE author's two PRs on a file DO collide (2nd → waiting + collision_held). AI fleets commonly share a single GitHub login, so the old 'count(DISTINCT agent_id) >= 2' banner showed 'All clear' at the exact moment Veripsa was holding a PR in line — the dashboard contradicting the gate. Fix: 'count(DISTINCT change_id) >= 2' + a changes_count field. Proven on the REAL gate + REAL surface (db/schema.sql): (A) two same-author PRs → 2nd 'waiting' AND server.py in contended with changes_count==2/waiting==1; (B) CONTROL load-bearing: that row has agents==1 so the old agent-based HAVING would have excluded it (not a no-op); (C) cross-agent two authors still surface (agents==2); (D) a single in-flight change is never contended (no false alarm)" "the live Now banner surfaces a file with >=2 in-flight CHANGES even under one shared login (gate-consistent), keeps cross-agent, no single-change false alarm" 20
